 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "Draw branches for each stage/event",
   "Write probabilities on each branch (must sum to 1 from each node)",
   "Multiply along a complete path for P(A AND B)",
   "Add paths together for P(A OR B)",
   "For without replacement, adjust the denominator"
  ],
  "title": "How to Use Tree Diagrams",
  "content": "<p>Probability ranges from 0 (impossible) to 1 (certain). \\(P(\\text{event}) = \\frac{\\text{favourable outcomes}}{\\text{total outcomes}}\\). The probability of something NOT happening: \\(P(A') = 1 - P(A)\\).</p><p>For <strong>combined events</strong>, use a <strong>tree diagram</strong>: each branch shows an outcome with its probability. Branches from the same point must sum to 1.</p><p><strong>AND rule:</strong> multiply along branches. <strong>OR rule:</strong> add the results of different paths.</p><p>With <strong>replacement</strong>: probabilities stay the same. <strong>Without replacement</strong>: probabilities change (denominator decreases by 1).</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>A bag has 3 red and 5 blue. Two balls drawn without replacement. Find P(both red).</strong></p><p>P(R then R) = \\(\\frac{3}{8} \\times \\frac{2}{7} = \\frac{6}{56} = \\frac{3}{28}\\)</p>"
 },
